{
  "kind": "callback",
  "source": "Numerics/Mathematics/{Root Finding/Test_Brent.cs, Differentiation/Test_Differentiation.cs, Integration/Test_AdaptiveGaussKronrod.cs}",
  "reference": "Numerics @ 2a0357a. Runs corehydro::numerics::support::run_callback (core/include/corehydro/numerics/support/callback_runner.hpp), group \"math\", against the callback named by `construct.callback` -- a function each of the four runners writes itself as a native closure (a C++ lambda, an R closure, a Python lambda, a C# delegate), so every case exercises the real host-language callback path the runner's guard exists to protect. NOTE the catalog names here are NOT the `optimizer`-kind catalog's: `Diff_FXYZ` is Test_Differentiation.FXYZ (x^3 + y^4 + z^5), not the unrelated TestFunctions.FXYZ the optimizer fixtures use. Every expected value and tolerance is the upstream MSTest `Assert.AreEqual(expected, actual, delta)` literal, transcribed verbatim, EXCEPT the assertions whose `source` opens with EMITTER-READ: no upstream test reads AdaptiveGaussKronrod's FunctionEvaluations, StandardError or Status, so those are read off the REAL C# library through tools/oracle_emitter instead. Neither kind is ever a value computed by this repo's own C++. `Quad_Peak` is likewise a corehydro addition rather than an upstream integrand: every Integrands.cs function the upstream tests integrate converges on the first whole-interval evaluation at 21 function evaluations, so without it the subdividing branch of the recursion has no oracle at all.",
  "callbacks": {
    "Root_Quadratic": "f(x) = x^2 - 2  [Mathematics/Root Finding/TestFunctions.Quadratic]",
    "Root_Cubic": "f(x) = x^3 - x - 1  [Mathematics/Root Finding/TestFunctions.Cubic]",
    "Diff_FX": "f(x) = x^3  [Test_Differentiation.FX]",
    "Diff_FXY": "f(x, y) = x^2 * y^3  [Test_Differentiation.FXY]",
    "Diff_FXYZ": "f(x, y, z) = x^3 + y^4 + z^5  [Test_Differentiation.FXYZ]",
    "Diff_FH": "f(x, y) = x^3 - 2xy - y^6  [Test_Differentiation.FH]",
    "Quad_FX3": "f(x) = x^3  [Mathematics/Integration/Integrands.FX3]",
    "Quad_Cosine": "f(x) = cos(x)  [Mathematics/Integration/Integrands.Cosine]",
    "Quad_Sine": "f(x) = sin(x)  [Mathematics/Integration/Integrands.Sine]",
    "Quad_FXX": "f(x) = 0.5 + 24x + 3x^2  [Mathematics/Integration/Integrands.FXX]",
    "Quad_FXXX": "f(x) = 0.5 + 24x + 3x^2 + 8x^3  [Mathematics/Integration/Integrands.FXXX]",
    "Quad_Peak": "f(x) = 1 / (1 + 1e4 * x^2)  [corehydro addition, NOT an upstream integrand -- see quadrature_peak_subdivides]"
  },
  "cases": [
