        { "method": "value", "args": [1], "expected": 21, "mode": "abs", "tol": 0, "source": "Test_AdaptiveGaussKronrod.Test_FX3, FunctionEvaluations read off the driven C# AdaptiveGaussKronrod: the G10K21 rule is exact for a cubic, so the whole-interval evaluation (1 centre + 10 symmetric pairs) converges with no subdivision" },
        { "method": "value", "args": [2], "expected": 0.0, "mode": "abs", "tol": 0, "source": "EMITTER-READ, no upstream test literal: StandardError read off the driven C# AdaptiveGaussKronrod. Exactly zero, and not by accident -- G10K21 is exact for a cubic, so the Gauss and Kronrod estimates agree to the last bit, the one accumulated squared error is 0, and no subdivision happens. Compare quadrature_peak_subdivides, where it is not" },
        { "method": "status", "expected": "Success", "source": "Test_AdaptiveGaussKronrod.Test_FX3, Status read off the driven C# AdaptiveGaussKronrod after Integrate()" }
